# Frosty Stress Test Suite

> **Purpose**: Verify Frosty behaves like a production assistant under all edge cases  
> **Target Endpoint**: `POST /chat` and `GET /health`

---

## 1. Long Conversation Memory (50+ Messages)

### Test 1.1 — Sliding Window Retention
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Send 50 sequential messages to the same `session_id`. Message #1: `"My name is Ayush"`. Messages #2–49: random chitchat. Message #50: `"What is my name?"` |
| **Expected** | Reply references "Ayush" — retrieved from user profile memory even though message #1 is outside the 10-message window |
| **Failure** | Bot says "I don't know your name" or hallucinates a different name |

### Test 1.2 — Context Coherence at Window Boundary
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Send 12 messages. Messages #1–2 discuss "Project Alpha deadline is March 15". Messages #3–12 are unrelated. Message #13: `"When is the Project Alpha deadline?"` |
| **Expected** | Bot recalls "March 15" via conversation summary (generated after 20+ messages) or profile memory |
| **Failure** | Bot loses context and cannot answer — summary was not injected |

---

## 2. Conversation Summarization Trigger

### Test 2.1 — Summary Generation at 20+ Messages
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Send exactly 21 messages to a session. After message #21, query DB: `SELECT summary FROM conversation_summary WHERE session_id = ?` |
| **Expected** | Summary exists, is non-empty, and preserves key facts from the conversation |
| **Failure** | Summary is NULL or empty — [maybe_summarize_and_prune()](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/memory/summary.py#164-182) did not trigger |

### Test 2.2 — History Pruning
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | After test 2.1, query DB: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM conversation_memory WHERE session_id = ?` |
| **Expected** | Count is ≤ 10 (pruned to last 10 messages) |
| **Failure** | Count is > 10 — [prune_old_history()](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/memory/summary.py#124-162) did not execute |

### Test 2.3 — Summary Injection After Pruning
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | After pruning, send `"Summarize what we discussed"` |
| **Expected** | Bot responds with accurate summary from stored [conversation_summary](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/session_store.py#161-199) |
| **Failure** | Bot says "We haven't discussed anything" — summary not injected into LLM context |

---

## 3. Multi-Step Email Confirmation

### Test 3.1 — Happy Path
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Message 1: `"Send an email to test@example.com Subject: Hello Message: Hi there"` → Message 2: `"yes"` |
| **Expected** | Message 1 returns confirmation prompt with `awaiting_confirmation=True`. Message 2 returns `"Email sent successfully."` |
| **Failure** | Email not sent, or confirmation not recognized |

### Test 3.2 — Cancel Flow
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Message 1: `"Send email to test@example.com Subject: Test Message: Body"` → Message 2: `"no"` |
| **Expected** | Returns `"Email cancelled."`, `awaiting_confirmation` set to `False`, `pending_action_data` cleared |
| **Failure** | Action still pending after cancel — [clear_pending_action()](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/session_store.py#418-449) not called |

### Test 3.3 — Invalid Confirmation Input
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Message 1: trigger email flow → Message 2: `"maybe"` |
| **Expected** | Returns `"Please reply with yes or no."`, state stays `awaiting_confirmation=True` |
| **Failure** | State gets corrupted or action executes without explicit yes |

### Test 3.4 — Pending Action Persistence
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Trigger email flow, then query DB for `pending_action_data` |
| **Expected** | JSONB contains `{"recipient": "...", "subject": "...", "body": "..."}` and `action_pending=TRUE` |
| **Failure** | `pending_action_data` is NULL — [set_pending_action()](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/session_store.py#337-372) not called |

---

## 4. Tool Retry Logic

### Test 4.1 — Email Retry on Transient Failure
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Temporarily set `SMTP_HOST` to an invalid host. Trigger email confirmation with `"yes"` |
| **Expected** | Logs show 2 retry attempts. Response: `"Failed to send email: {reason}. Please try again."` |
| **Failure** | Crashes with unhandled exception, or retries indefinitely |

### Test 4.2 — Calendar Retry on Transient Failure
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Temporarily invalidate Google credentials. Send meeting scheduling request |
| **Expected** | Logs show 2 retry attempts. Response: `"Failed to schedule meeting: {reason}. Please try again."` |
| **Failure** | Unhandled crash or `500` error returned to client |

### Test 4.3 — Successful Retry After First Failure
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Mock [send_email](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/email_tool.py#19-72) to fail on first call, succeed on second |
| **Expected** | Logs show `attempt=1/2 error=...` then `attempt=2/2 success`. Email delivered |
| **Failure** | Gives up after first failure despite having retries remaining |

---

## 5. Calendar Scheduling Flow

### Test 5.1 — Complete Meeting Scheduling
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `"Schedule a meeting titled Project Review on 2026-03-15 at 10:00 with Rahul"` |
| **Expected** | Returns `intent: "schedule_meeting"` with Google Calendar event link in reply |
| **Failure** | Missing fields error, or calendar API failure without retry |

### Test 5.2 — Missing Fields
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `"Schedule a meeting tomorrow"` (no time, title, or participant) |
| **Expected** | Returns prompt asking for missing fields: date, time, title, participant |
| **Failure** | Attempts to create event with null fields, crashes |

### Test 5.3 — Date Format Variations
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Try each: `"2026-03-15"`, `"15-03-2026"`, `"03/15/2026"` with time `"2:00 PM"` |
| **Expected** | All formats parsed correctly, events created |
| **Failure** | Certain date formats cause `ValueError` |

---

## 6. Voice Pipeline (STT → Tool → TTS)

### Test 6.1 — Audio Input to Text Response
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `{"session_id": "v1", "audio": "<valid_base64_wav>", "voice_response": false}` |
| **Expected** | [transcribe_audio()](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive/Desktop/frosty-langgraph/tools/voice_tool.py#7-59) converts to text, LLM processes, returns text `reply` with empty `audio_response` |
| **Failure** | Returns `"Could not process the provided input."` — Whisper STT failed |

### Test 6.2 — Audio Input to Audio Response
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `{"session_id": "v2", "audio": "<valid_base64_wav>", "voice_response": true}` |
| **Expected** | Full pipeline: STT → LLM → TTS. Response contains non-empty `audio_response` and `audio_mime: "audio/wav"` |
| **Failure** | `audio_response` is empty despite `voice_response=true` |

### Test 6.3 — Invalid Audio Base64
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `{"session_id": "v3", "audio": "not-valid-base64!!!"}` |
| **Expected** | Caught by error handler, returns `intent: "error"` with user-friendly message |
| **Failure** | Unhandled `ValueError` crashes the endpoint |

