## 7. Interrupt During Pending Action

### Test 7.1 — Normal Chat During Pending Email
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Step 1: Trigger email flow (`awaiting_confirmation=True`). Step 2: Send `"What's the weather?"` instead of yes/no |
| **Expected** | Confirmation guard catches all input — returns `"Please reply with yes or no."` |
| **Failure** | Message bypasses confirmation guard and enters normal chat flow |

### Test 7.2 — New Email Request During Pending Email
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Step 1: Trigger email flow. Step 2: Send `"Send email to other@test.com Subject: New Message: Different"` |
| **Expected** | Confirmation guard intercepts — does NOT start a new email flow while one is pending |
| **Failure** | Overwrites pending action data, corrupting the first email |

---

## 8. Session Isolation

### Test 8.1 — Cross-Session Memory Isolation
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Session A: `"My name is Alice"`. Session B: `"What is my name?"` |
| **Expected** | Session B does NOT know "Alice" — each session has independent memory |
| **Failure** | Session B leaks data from Session A |

### Test 8.2 — Cross-Session State Isolation
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Session A: trigger email flow (`awaiting_confirmation=True`). Session B: send `"yes"` |
| **Expected** | Session B processes "yes" as normal chat (no pending action in its state) |
| **Failure** | Session B executes Session A's pending email |

### Test 8.3 — Concurrent Sessions
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Fire 5 concurrent requests with different `session_id`s, each asking different questions |
| **Expected** | Each session receives independent, correct responses. No cross-contamination |
| **Failure** | Responses mixed up, or database deadlock |

---

## 9. Rate Limiting

### Test 9.1 — Under Limit
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Send 19 requests in 1 minute with the same `session_id` |
| **Expected** | All 19 return normal responses |
| **Failure** | Premature rate limit trigger |

### Test 9.2 — At Limit
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Send 21 requests in 1 minute with the same `session_id` |
| **Expected** | First 20 succeed. Request #21 returns `{"intent": "error", "reply": "Too many requests. Please slow down."}` |
| **Failure** | Request #21 succeeds, or rate limit triggers too early |

### Test 9.3 — Window Reset
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Send 20 requests, wait 61 seconds, send request #21 |
| **Expected** | Request #21 succeeds — window has reset |
| **Failure** | Still rate-limited after window expiry |

### Test 9.4 — Cross-Session Independence
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | Session A: send 20 requests (hit limit). Session B: send 1 request |
| **Expected** | Session B's request succeeds — rate limit is per-session |
| **Failure** | Session B is also rate-limited |

---

## 10. Continuous Voice Mode

### Test 10.1 — Flag Pass-Through
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `{"session_id": "c1", "message": "Hello", "voice_response": true, "continuous_mode": true}` |
| **Expected** | Response includes `"continuous": true` alongside `audio_response` |
| **Failure** | `continuous` field missing from response |

### Test 10.2 — Flag Defaults to False
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `{"session_id": "c2", "message": "Hello"}` (no `continuous_mode` field) |
| **Expected** | Response includes `"continuous": false` (or field absent) |
| **Failure** | `continuous` defaults to `true` when not specified |

### Test 10.3 — Continuous Mode Without Voice
| Field | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Input** | `{"session_id": "c3", "message": "Hello", "voice_response": false, "continuous_mode": true}` |
| **Expected** | Normal text response with empty `audio_response` and `"continuous": true` |
| **Failure** | TTS triggered despite `voice_response=false` |

